# On by default in every build made from this repository: the legal-documents notice (src/lib/Others/Legal.svelte)
# does not replace the app. To opt out, set VITE_RISU_LEGAL_CONFIGURED to an empty value in the build environment
# (Vite gives variables already present in the environment priority over this file), or put
# VITE_RISU_LEGAL_CONFIGURED= in an untracked .env.production.local, which loads after this file. Windows cmd
# cannot hold an empty variable, so there the .env.production.local file is the way.
# Keep this default out of .env, .env.local and .env.test*: the test run loads those and must see it unset.
VITE_RISU_LEGAL_CONFIGURED=TRUE
